  "summary": "Senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore of the Nick Xenophon Team has announced her resignation from the Australian Senate after discovering she holds dual British citizenship by descent through her mother. Kakoschke-Moore was born in Darwin in 1985 and believed she was not British based on earlier advice from the British embassy in Oman. However, she recently received confirmation from the UK Home Office and a barrister that she acquired British citizenship through her mother, who was born in Singapore in 1957 and obtained UK citizenship in 1983. Kakoschke-Moore expressed surprise and heartbreak at the discovery, describing it as completely unexpected. She plans to request the High Court determine how her Senate vacancy will be filled and intends to continue pursuing political office with the NXT party, hoping to return to the Senate. Party leader Nick Xenophon stated he is devastated by her departure but believes her political career is not over. A recount of the 2016 Senate election would likely see NXT candidate Tim Storrer elected to fill the position, though preliminary legal advice suggests the seat may not be filled through a recount, with Xenophon describing the situation as uncharted legal territory following a recent High Court decision."
